   "line": 4,
   "text": "On the wheel, one thousand hertz turns forty-five degrees per sample. The echo sits four steps behind, a half lap, and pulls against the tone. At two thousand hertz it sits a full lap behind, right on top. Walk up through the tones, and the gain rises and falls. That's a ripple.",
