  {
   "line": 6,
   "text": "You never see the echo alone, though. The voice is loud near seven hundred hertz, quiet near three thousand, and the echo multiplies it. So the ripple swings by a hundred on the hump, and by one in the valley. Take the log, and multiplied turns into plus. Now it swings one point one everywhere. That's the log spectrum.",
